1: # Design Patterns
2: 
3: Common design patterns for building robust Flutter applications.
4: 
5: ## Command Pattern
6: 
7: Encapsulates actions as objects with state management and Result handling.
8: 
9: ### Purpose
10: - Encapsulate complex logic
11: - Expose running and error states
12: - Prevent multiple simultaneous executions
13: - Type-safe error handling with Result type
14: 
15: ### Implementation
16: 
17: See `command.dart` asset for template implementation. Adapt imports and naming
18: to the target project before copying it into app code.
19: 
20: **Usage:**
21: 
22: ```dart
23: class MyViewModel extends ChangeNotifier {
24:   // Command without arguments
25:   Command0<void> get loadData => _loadDataCommand;
26:   late final _loadDataCommand = Command0<void>(_loadData);
27: 
28:   // Command with one argument
29:   Command1<void, String> get saveItem => _saveCommand;
30:   late final _saveCommand = Command1<void, String>(_saveItem);
31: 
32:   Future<Result<void>> _loadData() async {
33:     // Logic here
34:     return Result.ok(null);
35:   }
36: 
37:   Future<Result<void>> _saveItem(String item) async {
38:     // Logic here
39:     return Result.ok(null);
40:   }
41: }
42: ```
43: 
44: **In View:**
45: 
46: ```dart
47: ListenableBuilder(
48:   listenable: viewModel.loadData,
49:   builder: (context, child) {
50:     if (viewModel.loadData.running) {
51:       return CircularProgressIndicator();
52:     }
53:     if (viewModel.loadData.error) {
54:       return Text('Error: ${viewModel.loadData.result?.asError.error}');
55:     }
56:     return ElevatedButton(
57:       onPressed: () => viewModel.loadData.execute(),
58:       child: Text('Load Data'),
59:     );
60:   },
61: );
62: ```
63: 
64: ### Benefits
65: - Prevents double-taps
66: - Exposes loading, error, success states
67: - Type-safe Result handling
68: - Encapsulates complex logic
69: 
70: ## Result Type
71: 
72: Type-safe error handling without exceptions.
73: 
74: ### Purpose
75: - Represent success or failure states
76: - Type-safe error handling
77: - Avoid try-catch blocks
78: - Clear error propagation
79: 
80: ### Implementation
81: 
82: See `result.dart` asset for template implementation. Use it only when the app
83: does not already have an equivalent typed error/result abstraction.
84: 
85: **Usage:**
86: 
87: ```dart
88: Future<Result<User>> fetchUser(String id) async {
89:   try {
90:     final response = await http.get('/users/$id');
91:     final user = User.fromJson(response.body);
92:     return Result.ok(user);
93:   } catch (e) {
94:     return Result.error(Exception('Failed to fetch user: $e'));
95:   }
96: }
97: 
98: // Consume result
99: final result = await fetchUser('123');
100: switch (result) {
101:   case Ok():
102:     print('User: ${result.value.name}');
103:   case Error():
104:     print('Error: ${result.error}');
105: }
106: ```
107: 
108: ### Benefits
109: - Explicit error handling
110: - Type-safe
111: - No uncaught exceptions
112: - Clear state representation
113: 
114: ## Repository Pattern
115: 
116: Abstraction over data sources providing single source of truth.
117: 
118: ### Purpose
119: - Hide data source complexity
120: - Provide single source of truth
121: - Enable caching and offline support
122: - Facilitate testing
123: 
124: ### Implementation
125: 
126: ```dart
127: class TodoRepository {
128:   final ApiService _apiService;
129:   final DatabaseService _databaseService;
130:   final BehaviorSubject<List<Todo>> _todos = BehaviorSubject.seeded([]);
131: 
132:   Stream<List<Todo>> get todos => _todos.stream;
133: 
134:   TodoRepository(this._apiService, this._databaseService) {
135:     _loadTodos();
136:   }
137: 
138:   Future<void> _loadTodos() async {
139:     try {
140:       final todos = await _databaseService.getTodos();
141:       _todos.add(todos);
142:       _refreshFromServer();
143:     } catch (e) {
144:       // Handle error
145:     }
146:   }
147: 
148:   Future<void> _refreshFromServer() async {
149:     try {
150:       final todos = await _apiService.fetchTodos();
151:       await _databaseService.saveTodos(todos);
152:       _todos.add(todos);
153:     } catch (e) {
154:       // Keep cached data on network error
155:     }
156:   }
157: 
158:   Future<Result<Todo>> addTodo(Todo todo) async {
159:     try {
160:       final savedTodo = await _apiService.createTodo(todo);
161:       await _databaseService.saveTodo(savedTodo);

161:       await _databaseService.saveTodo(savedTodo);
162:       final updated = [..._todos.value, savedTodo];
163:       _todos.add(updated);
164:       return Result.ok(savedTodo);
165:     } catch (e) {
166:       return Result.error(e is Exception ? e : Exception(e.toString()));
167:     }
168:   }
169: }
170: ```
171: 
172: ### Benefits
173: - Unified data access interface
174: - Caching layer
175: - Error handling centralized
176: - Easy to mock for testing
177: 
178: ## Optimistic UI
179: 
180: Update UI immediately, then sync with server.
181: 
182: ### Purpose
183: - Improve perceived performance
184: - Better user experience
185: - Handle network delays gracefully
186: 
187: ### Implementation
188: 
189: ```dart
190: class TodoViewModel extends ChangeNotifier {
191:   final TodoRepository _repository;
192:   List<Todo> _todos = [];
193: 
194:   TodoViewModel(this._repository);
195: 
196:   List<Todo> get todos => _todos;
197: 
198:   Command0<Todo> get addTodo => _addTodoCommand;
199:   late final _addTodoCommand = Command0<Todo>(_executeAddTodo);
200: 
201:   Future<Result<Todo>> _executeAddTodo() async {
202:     // Optimistic update
203:     final tempTodo = Todo(
204:       id: DateTime.now().millisecondsSinceEpoch.toString(),
205:       title: 'New Todo',
206:       isComplete: false,
207:     );
208:     _todos = [..._todos, tempTodo];
209:     notifyListeners();
210: 
211:     // Actual API call
212:     final result = await _repository.addTodo(tempTodo);
213: 
214:     if (result case Error()) {
215:       // Rollback on error
216:       _todos = _todos.where((t) => t.id != tempTodo.id).toList();
217:       notifyListeners();
218:       return result;
219:     }
220: 
221:     // Update with server response
222:     final serverTodo = result.asOk.value;
223:     _todos = _todos.map((t) => t.id == tempTodo.id ? serverTodo : t).toList();
224:     notifyListeners();
225: 
226:     return Result.ok(serverTodo);
227:   }
228: }
229: ```
230: 
231: ### Benefits
232: - Instant UI response
233: - Better perceived performance
234: - Graceful error handling with rollback
235: 
236: ## Offline-First
237: 
238: Cache data locally, sync when online.
239: 
240: ### Purpose
241: - Support offline usage
242: - Reduce network calls
243: - Improve performance
244: - Handle poor connectivity
245: 
246: ### Key Concepts
247: - Local cache as primary data source
248: - Background sync when online
249: - Optimistic updates with conflict resolution
250: - Network status monitoring
251: 
252: ### Implementation Pattern
253: 
254: ```dart
255: class TodoRepository {
256:   final ApiService _api;
257:   final LocalStorage _local;
258: 
259:   Stream<List<Todo>> get todos {
260:     // Stream from local cache (always available)
261:     return _local.todosStream;
262:   }
263: 
264:   Future<void> sync() async {
265:     if (!await _hasConnection()) return;
266: 
267:     final remote = await _api.getTodos();
268: 
269:     // Conflict resolution: remote wins
270:     await _local.saveTodos(remote);
271:   }
272: 
273:   Future<Result<Todo>> addTodo(Todo todo) async {
274:     // Save locally first (offline support)
275:     await _local.saveTodo(todo);
276: 
277:     // Sync when online
278:     if (await _hasConnection()) {
279:       final result = await _api.createTodo(todo);
280:       switch (result) {
281:         case Ok<Todo>():
282:           await _local.saveTodo(result.value);
283:           return result;
284:         case Error<Todo>():
285:           return result;
286:       }
287:     }
288: 
289:     return Result.ok(todo);
290:   }
291: }
292: ```
293: 
294: ## Dependency Injection
295: 
296: Provide dependencies externally rather than creating internally.
297: 
298: ### Purpose
299: - Testability (inject mocks)
300: - Loose coupling
301: - Flexibility (swap implementations)
302: - Clear dependencies
303: 
304: ### Implementation Patterns
305: 
306: **Constructor Injection:**
307: 
308: ```dart
309: class TodoViewModel extends ChangeNotifier {
310:   final TodoRepository _repository;
311: 
312:   TodoViewModel(this._repository);
313: }
314: ```
315: 
316: **Provider Setup:**
317: 
318: ```dart
319: void main() {
320:   final apiService = ApiService();
321:   final databaseService = DatabaseService();
322:   final repository = TodoRepository(apiService, databaseService);
323:   final viewModel = TodoViewModel(repository);
324: 
325:   runApp(
326:     MultiProvider(
327:       providers: [
328:         Provider<TodoRepository>.value(value: repository),
329:         ChangeNotifierProvider<TodoViewModel>.value(value: viewModel),
330:       ],

